<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE kinetica2-y2 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Kinetica-2 Y2 / Qianfan polar group (Jiuquan LA-140) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 15.00 s, kick 0.415 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.667, payload 6736 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=1.7884-0.008109*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: Kinetica-2 (Lijian-2, CAS Space) (sim/vehicles/kinetica2.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Kinetica-2 TIMELINE mode: thrust/Isp/GLOW/fairing/typical event times from huijiwiki (CAS Space sources) + zh.wikipedia YF-102; ALL propellant/dry masses DERIVED from burn x mdot and the published 0.92 structure coefficient. S1 burn 180 s is the derived upper bound (ASSUMED). UNTUNED: no altitude/range knots published; LOW confidence.
T0 = LL2 NET 2026-11-03T00:10:00Z (window 00:05-00:33Z, Go); SatNet News (unofficial) window BJT 3 Nov 08:00-09:00 (https://satnet.news/item/76103, /item/70043). LL2: &#x27;payload and LV identities highly uncertain&#x27;.
Event times = CAS Space TYPICAL Kinetica-2 sequence (Y1 documentary via huijiwiki), not this flight&#x27;s; S1 burn/sep ASSUMED. UNTUNED: no altitude/range knots exist to tune against.
Target (see launch config): insertion 500 km, apoapsis 500 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 186.58 deg; payload 6736 kg.
Pad: 40.817480N 100.219390E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-03T00:10:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: after final cutoff T+493.7 s the stage coasts (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model) to PAYLOAD DEPLOY T+515 s; rows after cutoff tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF deploy T+515 s (CAS Space typical sequence via huijiwiki: payload separation T+514.710 s (TYPICAL, not Y2-specific)): alt 499.59 km, osculating 495.2 x 505.6 km, i 94.266 deg.
POST-CUTOFF note: S2 second burn (restart 806.71 s, cutoff 811.71 s in the typical sequence) is after payload separation (disposal-class) and is not modelled.</description>
